    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "[[0,30], [5,10], [15,20]]  ->  false   (5-10 overlaps 0-30)\n[[7,10], [2,4]]            ->  true\n[[1,5], [5,8]]             ->  true    (one ends as the other starts)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: sort by start, then only neighbours can clash"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Two meetings overlap when each starts before the other ends. Checking every pair is O(n²). Instead, sort by start time. If every meeting starts no earlier than the **previous one ends**, the meetings form a chain in time — each finishes before the next begins — so no two can overlap at all. And if some meeting starts before the previous one ends, that's a clash. So one pass comparing each meeting with the one **just before it** decides the answer."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Brute force: check every pair"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function canAttendMeetings(intervals) {\n  for (let i = 0; i < intervals.length; i++) {\n    for (let j = i + 1; j < intervals.length; j++) {\n      const [a, b] = [intervals[i], intervals[j]];\n      if (a[0] < b[1] && b[0] < a[1]) return false;   // each starts before the other ends\n    }\n  }\n  return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def can_attend_meetings(intervals):\n    for i in range(len(intervals)):\n        for j in range(i + 1, len(intervals)):\n            a, b = intervals[i], intervals[j]\n            if a[0] < b[1] and b[0] < a[1]:   # each starts before the other ends\n                return False\n    return True"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "boolean canAttendMeetings(int[][] intervals) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < intervals.length; i++) {\n        for (int j = i + 1; j < intervals.length; j++) {\n            int[] a = intervals[i], b = intervals[j];\n            if (a[0] < b[1] && b[0] < a[1]) return false;   // each starts before the other ends\n        }\n    }\n    return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "bool canAttendMeetings(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < intervals.size(); i++) {\n        for (size_t j = i + 1; j < intervals.size(); j++) {\n            auto& a = intervals[i];\n            auto& b = intervals[j];\n            if (a[0] < b[1] && b[0] < a[1]) return false;   // each starts before the other ends\n        }\n    }\n    return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n²), space O(1).**"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Sort by start, compare neighbours"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "meeting-rooms",
      "caption": "After sorting by start, each meeting only needs checking against the one before it."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function canAttendMeetings(intervals) {\n  const sorted = [...intervals].sort((a, b) => a[0] - b[0]);   // by start time\n  for (let i = 1; i < sorted.length; i++) {\n    if (sorted[i][0] < sorted[i - 1][1]) return false;          // starts before the previous one ends\n  }\n  return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def can_attend_meetings(intervals):\n    s = sorted(intervals)                 # by start time\n    for i in range(1, len(s)):\n        if s[i][0] < s[i - 1][1]:         # starts before the previous one ends\n            return False\n    return True"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "boolean canAttendMeetings(int[][] intervals) {\n    int[][] sorted = intervals.clone();\n    Arrays.sort(sorted, (a, b) -> Integer.compare(a[0], b[0]));   // by start time\n    for (int i = 1; i < sorted.length; i++) {\n        if (sorted[i][0] < sorted[i - 1][1]) return false;         // starts before the previous one ends\n    }\n    return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "bool canAttendMeetings(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {\n    vector<vector<int>> sorted = intervals;\n    sort(sorted.begin(), sorted.end());                         // by start time\n    for (size_t i = 1; i < sorted.size(); i++) {\n        if (sorted[i][0] < sorted[i - 1][1]) return false;      // starts before the previous one ends\n    }\n    return true;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n log n), space O(n)** for the sorted copy (O(1) extra sorting in place)."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
