    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**No meetings or one** — true.",
        "**Touching meetings** — `[1,5]` and `[5,8]` don't overlap: use `<`, not `<=`.",
        "**Unsorted input** — the clash may be between meetings far apart in the input.",
        "**A long meeting covering others** — `[0,30]` swallows `[15,20]`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Meeting Rooms II** — how many rooms are needed when meetings may overlap. Two lessons on.",
        "**Merge Intervals** — sort by start, then merge overlapping neighbours (Arrays course).",
        "**Non-overlapping Intervals** — the fewest meetings to cancel so the rest fit. Next-but-one lesson."
      ]
    }
